From: Macron <macron@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: Report the driver versions of today for Windows 10
 and for NVIDIA's cards.

wined3d makes up the display driver's version from a table: 31.0.x.y on
Windows 10 and 11, and for every NVIDIA card since the GeForce 600 series
x.y = 15.3118, driver 531.18 of 2023. Drivers have been 32.0.x.y since
Windows 11 24H2 (WDDM 3.2), and games compare the number with the oldest
driver they accept.

Deadlock (Source 2) reads it through Direct3D 9's adapter identifier even
though it draws with Direct3D 11. With Macron's `dlss` switch DXMT answers
as an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090, and the game then opens on a box,
"Graphics Driver Out-of-Date" over a black screen, that has to be
clicked away at every start:

  Graphics driver is out of date.  Vendor 10de, 'NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090',
  version 31.0.13.783 < 32.0.15.8108

(13.783 is the table's GeForce 6 driver: wined3d did not know it was
meant to be an NVIDIA card at all. Macron's launcher now tells it, with
WINE_D3D_CONFIG's VideoPciVendorID and VideoPciDeviceID, when the switch
is on.)

The Windows 10 and 11 drivers are 32.0 now, and the NVIDIA entry is
15.9144, driver 591.44.
---
diff --git a/dlls/wined3d/directx.c b/dlls/wined3d/directx.c
index b8bd2c6..c5db501 100644
--- a/dlls/wined3d/directx.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/directx.c
@@ -318,7 +318,7 @@ static const struct driver_version_information driver_version_table[] =
     {DRIVER_NVIDIA_GEFORCE6,    DRIVER_MODEL_NT6X,  "nvd3dum.dll",     13,  783},
     {DRIVER_NVIDIA_GEFORCE8,    DRIVER_MODEL_NT6X,  "nvd3dum.dll",     13, 4052},
     {DRIVER_NVIDIA_FERMI,       DRIVER_MODEL_NT6X,  "nvd3dum.dll",     13, 9135},
-    {DRIVER_NVIDIA_KEPLER,      DRIVER_MODEL_NT6X,  "nvd3dum.dll",     15, 3118}, /* 531.18 */
+    {DRIVER_NVIDIA_KEPLER,      DRIVER_MODEL_NT6X,  "nvd3dum.dll",     15, 9144}, /* 591.44 */
 
     /* Red Hat */
     {DRIVER_REDHAT_VIRGL,       DRIVER_MODEL_GENERIC, "virgl.dll",      0,    0},
@@ -812,7 +812,8 @@ bool wined3d_driver_info_init(struct wined3d_driver_info *driver_info,
                 break;
 
             case 10:
-                driver_os_version = 31;
+                /* What drivers for Windows 10 and 11 have carried since 2024 (WDDM 3.2). */
+                driver_os_version = 32;
                 driver_model = DRIVER_MODEL_NT6X;
                 break;
 
